Research Note 1: AVM Data Suitability Framework

Title: Data Suitability as a Precondition for Reliable AVMs

Motivation

AVM performance is commonly associated with the availability of transaction data. However, evidence from Indian residential markets suggests that transaction volume alone is insufficient for reliable automated valuation. The limiting factor is the suitability of valuation data rather than its mere existence.

Core Proposition

> Reliable AVMs require data suitability rather than simply data availability.



Distinction

Data Availability

Number of property transactions

Geographic coverage

Market participation

Historical observations


Data Suitability

Verified arm's-length transaction prices

Standardised property characteristics

Persistent property identifiers

Longitudinal transaction histories

Data completeness

Timeliness

Cross-source consistency

Regulatory accessibility

Model validation capability


Implication

Markets may exhibit high transaction activity while remaining unsuitable for robust AVM deployment because the underlying valuation evidence lacks sufficient quality, standardisation or governance.

This reframes the research problem from "data sparsity" to "valuation data suitability."

Research Opportunity

Introduce Data Suitability as an antecedent of valuation uncertainty.

Conceptual chain

Market Observability
        ↓
Data Suitability
        ↓
Valuation Uncertainty
        ↓
Valuation Governance
        ↓
Credit Risk Decision


